---
import ArticleClosingNote from '@/components/articles/ArticleClosingNote.astro';
import { articleHref } from '@/domains/articles/catalog';

const prose = 'article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0';
const mapLink = 'text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]';
---

<section id="section-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Buy Your Visa on Arrival</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>I personally recommend buying your Visa on Arrival once you land in Bali instead of applying online beforehand. The Visa on Arrival is valid for 30 days, with the option to apply for an extension if you're planning to stay longer.</p>
    <p>During my trip, I met several travellers who experienced issues with their online applications and ended up having to pay for a new visa at the airport because the information couldn't be corrected. Personally, I'd rather spend a little extra time at the airport than risk paying twice.</p>
    <p>I arrived in Bali during the early hours of the morning and the process was surprisingly quick, so I didn't experience any long queues.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Get an eSIM Before You Arrive</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you're planning to use an eSIM, Airalo worked really well for me. I had reliable coverage across Bali and never experienced any connection issues, making it easy to navigate, book transport, and stay connected wherever I went.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Cash or Card?</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>I'd recommend arriving with a small amount of cash, but don't worry about carrying too much. During my trip, I was able to pay by card at every café I visited, which meant I didn't need to rely heavily on cash.</p>
    <p>One thing I always do is keep an eye on how much cash I have left towards the end of my trip. If I still have a fair amount a couple of days before flying home, I'll start using cash instead of my card so I don't end up bringing too much foreign currency back with me.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-insurance" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Travel Insurance</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>I'd highly recommend getting travel insurance before travelling to Bali. Hopefully, you won't need it, but it's one of those things you'll be glad to have if something unexpected happens, whether it's a medical emergency, lost luggage, or a cancelled flight.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Download Grab or Gojek</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you need to get around Bali, I'd recommend downloading Grab before you arrive. It's the app I used throughout my trip, and I found it reliable, affordable, and available almost everywhere I visited.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>My Bali Travel Pharmacy</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>As a pharmacist, I always travel with a small pharmacy kit. Fortunately, I rarely need any of it, but there are a few essentials I never leave home without.</p>
    <p>For Bali, I packed pain relief medication, probiotics, electrolytes, and mosquito repellent. I also ended up buying activated charcoal tablets from a local pharmacy after developing Bali Belly, and they were what helped me recover.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Don't Drink Tap Water</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>Tap water in Bali isn't considered safe to drink, so it's best to stick to bottled water throughout your trip. I'd also recommend using bottled water when brushing your teeth, just to help reduce the risk of stomach issues.</p>
    <p>If you'd like to read more about my experience with Bali Belly, what helped me recover, and a few simple ways to reduce your risk, you can read my <a href={articleHref('bali-belly')} class={mapLink}>full guide here</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-6" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class={prose}>
    <ArticleClosingNote label="Before you go">
      <p>Every traveller has a different experience, but these are the things that worked well for me during my time in Bali. I hope they help you feel a little more prepared and make your trip a little easier.</p>
    </ArticleClosingNote>
  </div>
</section>
